1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,604
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:30,363
[Cora] <i>Their worst act of corruption</i>

6
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:34,075
<i>was when Mrs. Emilia founded</i>
<i>the Women's Union.</i>

7
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:35,869
[Camia] <i>We promise to protect you</i>

8
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:38,163
<i>if you testify against the Ardientes.</i>

9
00:00:38,246 --> 00:00:40,749
[Cora] <i>Testify? You didn't say</i>
<i>anything about that.</i>

10
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:43,418
<i>-Wait, where are you taking me?</i>
<i>-The mayor is dangerous.</i>

11
00:00:43,501 --> 00:00:45,837
<i>That is why we moved him</i>
<i>to the psychiatric ward.</i>

12
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:49,215
<i>I think I will have to take</i>
<i>my grandson out of this place.</i>

13
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,593
<i>Arnaldo, you'll get better. But not here.</i>

14
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:54,137
<i>You will spend time in our rest house.</i>

15
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,930
[Arnaldo] <i>I want Ivy to come with me.</i>

16
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:58,266
<i>Where do these hallucinations come from?</i>

17
00:00:58,349 --> 00:01:01,186
[Dr. Go] <i>Sometimes, there are truths</i>

18
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:03,855
<i>buried in our subconscious.</i>

19
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:05,482
[Ivy] <i>I'm leaving this place.</i>

20
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:07,567
<i>Arnaldo tried to kill me last night.</i>

21
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:08,735
<i>Someone tried to choke me,</i>

22
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:10,904
<i>and I know that it was Arnaldo.</i>

23
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:14,074
<i>Ivy, just tell me if you need me</i>
<i>and I'll be there.</i>

24
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:17,744
[Ivy] <i>No, Diego. I have to know</i>
<i>what's happening to Arnaldo.</i>

25
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:19,913
<i>I have to know why he's acting strange.</i>

26
00:01:19,996 --> 00:01:22,457
[inner voice] <i>There's only one way</i>
<i>to end your suffering.</i>

27
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,917
<i>Kill Ivy Aguas!</i>

28
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,337
<i>No. Stop! No! No!</i>

29
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:35,136
[foreboding music playing]

30
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:50,985
[doctor] <i>Julio, I'm sorry.</i>

31
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:54,114
<i>But your cancer is back.</i>

32
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:56,950
<i>Bone cancer is very dangerous.</i>

33
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:59,244
<i>Are you saying my days are numbered?</i>

34
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:01,913
<i>Julio, we have to conduct more tests.</i>

35
00:02:06,042 --> 00:02:09,045
[foreboding music playing]

36
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:16,553
[Julio] <i>My time is ending,</i>
<i>and yours is just about to start.</i>

37
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:20,890
<i>You've grown up to be a fine gentleman,</i>

38
00:02:20,974 --> 00:02:24,853
<i>and I'm so blessed</i>
<i>to have a grandson like you</i>

39
00:02:24,936 --> 00:02:27,147
<i>because of your respect for me.</i>

40
00:02:27,772 --> 00:02:31,317
-[gunshots]
-[screams]

41
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:34,195
[Raul] <i>Son! Help! Help!</i>

42
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:37,907
[Julio] <i>You are the son that I never had.</i>

43
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,785
<i>I'm so proud of you.</i>

44
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:05,143
[dark music playing]

45
00:03:09,647 --> 00:03:11,399
Emilia, Claire…

46
00:03:12,358 --> 00:03:15,987
Pack your things.
We're leaving this house.

47
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:18,406
-What?
-Huh?!

48
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:23,953
Yes. I don't want
Arnaldo to come home here.

49
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:27,749
This house holds too many bad memories.

50
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:30,335
Mostly, from you.

51
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:34,297
So, it's better for Arnaldo
not to stay here,

52
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:36,007
so he can recover faster.

53
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:39,344
But, Papa, we can't just
pack up and leave!

54
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:41,346
I've never known you as someone

55
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:43,723
who makes a decision on a whim, Julio.

56
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:45,600
And you never will!

57
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:50,063
Because, unlike you women,
I only make right decisions.

58
00:03:50,146 --> 00:03:52,649
-Oh.
-Papa, what is this about?

59
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:54,609
This has always been our home.

60
00:03:55,109 --> 00:03:59,364
Please, there's no sense
in being sentimental right now.

61
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:03,534
You know how I hate repeating myself,

62
00:04:03,618 --> 00:04:05,411
so, please, don't make me.

63
00:04:05,703 --> 00:04:08,164
But, why are we moving?
Where will we move, Papa?

64
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:10,917
This house is our seat of power.

65
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:14,295
And that is why I will never
leave my legacy to you.

66
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:16,798
Because you do not have the brains

67
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:18,967
nor the gumption of a true Ardiente!

68
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,511
You know what? This house is just that…

69
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:23,137
another house.

70
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:24,681
A roof over our heads.

71
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:26,683
No more, no less!

72
00:04:27,558 --> 00:04:31,771
Okay. No more, no less, Papa. Fine.

73
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:42,365
[Julio] <i>The true power of the Ardientes</i>

74
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:44,200
<i>isn't where this mansion is.</i>

75
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:53,793
<i>Wherever we breathe, lead,</i>
<i>and are held in high regard,</i>

76
00:04:53,876 --> 00:04:56,379
<i>is where the Ardientes' power really is.</i>

77
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:11,394
<i>All of us Ardientes…</i>
<i>I, and eventually Arnaldo,</i>

78
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:13,646
<i>will make this family a powerful one.</i>

79
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:16,316
<i>I have to make sure</i>

80
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:20,903
<i>that Arnaldo will fulfill</i>
<i>his role as my living legacy.</i>

81
00:05:22,905 --> 00:05:25,908
[tense music playing]

82
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:56,814
[tense music continues playing]

83
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:14,957
Emilia, Claire, this will be
our new home sweet home.

84
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:18,127
I'll be at my office.

85
00:06:18,544 --> 00:06:20,963
Bring all my personal belongings there.

86
00:06:37,563 --> 00:06:39,148
I didn't know about this place.

87
00:06:39,982 --> 00:06:43,694
Well, Auntie, I may have a lot of secrets,

88
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:47,115
but Papa definitely
has more secrets than I do.

89
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:51,244
This is one of his properties
that I didn't know about.

90
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:52,870
I'm sure there's more.

91
00:06:53,621 --> 00:06:56,791
So… does Raul know this place?

92
00:06:57,041 --> 00:06:58,209
Well, Auntie, I don't care.

93
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:00,837
Papa may have succeeded
in bringing us here…

94
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:03,172
but I'll still push through with my plans.

95
00:07:04,215 --> 00:07:06,843
Anyway, I have to go.
I'm going to visit Arnaldo.

96
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:07,969
Bye, Auntie.

97
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:16,853
Arnaldo is unstable,
and he's been throwing a fit!

98
00:07:16,936 --> 00:07:18,438
I need an ambulance!

99
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:21,816
No, I can't wait!
I need that ambulance now!

100
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:26,529
Ivy! Surprise!

101
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:28,156
Emilia!

102
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:33,661
How are you?

103
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:36,539
Oh, Arnaldo!

104
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:38,958
Hon, surprise! Your mom's here.

105
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:41,127
How are you? Are you feeling better?

106
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:43,921
Arnaldo.

107
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:49,260
I'm… I'm… I'm sorry.

108
00:07:49,343 --> 00:07:50,887
I'm just a little over the edge.

109
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:53,222
I know, you've been like this
since last night.

110
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:55,516
Yeah, maybe because of the medicine.

111
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,893
It's giving me mood swings.

112
00:07:57,643 --> 00:08:01,564
Seriously?! I'm just here
to check on you and Ivy!

113
00:08:01,981 --> 00:08:02,899
Oh.

114
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,860
Is the mansion
becoming too boring for you?

115
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:07,361
Is that why you're bothering us?

116
00:08:07,445 --> 00:08:09,822
-Arnaldo…
-Ivy and I are fine.

117
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:13,242
That's all you have to know.
Now, please leave.

118
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:18,915
I'll be right there, hon.

119
00:08:39,810 --> 00:08:42,772
[dark music playing]

120
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:50,238
[mouthing words]

121
00:08:50,821 --> 00:08:52,615
[phone rings]

122
00:08:59,205 --> 00:09:01,332
-Grandpa?
<i>-Hello, Arnaldo.</i>

123
00:09:01,415 --> 00:09:04,710
How are you? Better? Are you okay?

124
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:06,671
<i>Well…</i>

125
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:10,591
<i>Has your mom been there yet?</i>
<i>Well, I was just…</i>

126
00:09:10,883 --> 00:09:14,095
…reading the papers,
and it says here that…

127
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:17,139
everybody's waiting for you to get well.

128
00:09:17,515 --> 00:09:20,101
<i>So, get well soon.</i>

129
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:24,522
Get well because we still have
a full campaign ahead of us.

130
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:27,149
[groans]

131
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:30,361
[dark music playing]

132
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:35,741
I'm… I'm far from okay,

133
00:09:35,825 --> 00:09:36,909
<i>Grandpa.</i>

134
00:09:38,661 --> 00:09:40,288
I'm far from okay.

135
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:47,920
[dark music continues playing]

136
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,013
[line rings]

137
00:09:57,763 --> 00:09:58,931
Hello, Emilia, I have a--

138
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:00,057
[phone beeps]

139
00:10:14,655 --> 00:10:17,116
DIEGO TORILLO FILES CASE ANEW VERSUS
BROTHER, MAYOR ARNALDO TORILLO

140
00:10:17,199 --> 00:10:18,326
[scoffs]

141
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:22,705
He's really getting on my nerves.

142
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:29,253
[line rings]

143
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:33,716
Colonel Sanggano…

144
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:40,765
Teach that bastard, Diego, a lesson.

145
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:44,894
[tense music playing]

146
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:55,112
[inner voice] <i>You really are nuts!</i>

147
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:58,282
<i>She doesn't love you!</i>
<i>She's just using you!</i>

148
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:00,326
No… Stop it! No.

149
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:03,287
[groaning]

150
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:07,041
[groans] I don't believe you.

151
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:10,419
No. I'm gonna get better.

152
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:13,255
I'll get better! I'll get better!

153
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:17,802
[grunting and screaming]

154
00:11:18,427 --> 00:11:19,428
[grunts]

155
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:21,389
[inner voice] <i>You see?</i>

156
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:24,100
<i>That's what you're good at… playing dumb!</i>

157
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:27,436
<i>Well, since you can't kill Ivy…</i>

158
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:31,315
<i>why don't you kill yourself instead?</i>

159
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:35,653
[no audible dialogue]

160
00:11:36,862 --> 00:11:40,533
Get out! You're not here!
Don't listen to him! No!

161
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:43,536
[Jepoy] Hold on, what is that?

162
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:45,830
Someone sent it for Mr. Diego.

163
00:11:46,914 --> 00:11:48,040
Diego? I'll give this to him.

164
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:50,751
-Diego.
-You have a gift, Batch!

165
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:56,090
Hey, do you know who it's from?

166
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:58,467
No, someone just handed it to me.

167
00:12:02,513 --> 00:12:03,597
[Anna] Diego, wait…

168
00:12:03,681 --> 00:12:05,057
That came from the Ardientes.

169
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:07,309
Whatever's in there
is dangerous. Don't open it.

170
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:09,645
How will we know if we don't open it?

171
00:12:09,728 --> 00:12:10,729
[murmurs]

172
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:15,734
[Anna] Don't open it, Diego!
You have to be careful!

173
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:17,611
-Don't worry…
-What's inside?

174
00:12:18,696 --> 00:12:19,989
Diego, what if a bomb's in there?

175
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:26,120
[suspenseful music playing]

176
00:12:35,713 --> 00:12:38,674
-[snake hisses]
-[screams]

177
00:12:38,757 --> 00:12:42,887
[Anna] Jepoy! Jepoy! Jepoy!

178
00:12:43,554 --> 00:12:46,432
[snake hisses]

179
00:12:48,267 --> 00:12:49,477
[Fernan] Be careful, Diego.

180
00:12:53,522 --> 00:12:57,276
-Don't! Jepoy, wait.
-Stand back… Be careful!

181
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:01,197
-Diego, be careful!
-Be careful, Batch.

182
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:04,617
[suspenseful music playing]

183
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:17,838
[screams]

184
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:20,424
[Pandoy] Diego! Easy.

185
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:24,345
[Fernan] Get the box! Get the box!

186
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:25,846
-Look at it!
-What?!

187
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:27,848
-Jepoy, put it back.
-Slowly.

188
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:29,225
-[Anna] Be careful!
-Put it there, Jepoy.

189
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:30,476
[Anna] Please be careful.

190
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:35,981
Be careful.

191
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:39,360
-Easy.
-Be careful.

192
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,904
-Hold it there.
-Got it?

193
00:13:42,613 --> 00:13:44,865
Get that snake a round-trip ticket

194
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:46,408
so we can send it back to Julio Ardiente!

195
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:48,327
-See if he likes it!
-That's right.

196
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:52,623
Next time, don't just receive packages

197
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:54,166
unless they're from
the members of this party.

198
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:55,125
Do you understand?

199
00:13:55,209 --> 00:13:56,835
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am. Yes, ma'am.

200
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:01,423
[Julio] <i>This is a cobra,</i>

201
00:14:01,507 --> 00:14:04,385
<i>one of the most poisonous</i>
<i>snakes in the world.</i>

202
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:08,222
<i>If you're reading this,</i>
<i>it means you got lucky.</i>

203
00:14:08,305 --> 00:14:11,767
<i>But I'll make sure you won't</i>
<i>be as lucky next time.</i>

204
00:14:21,151 --> 00:14:22,695
Just wait for me out here.

205
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:27,074
Miss, is this the end of the queue?

206
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:28,659
-Yes it is, ma'am.
-Thank you.

207
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:30,870
[woman] Next, please.

208
00:14:34,039 --> 00:14:36,542
[phone rings]

209
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:41,380
-Hello, Diego?
<i>-Hello, Auntie?</i>

210
00:14:41,463 --> 00:14:43,048
Be careful over there.

211
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:45,551
Julio Ardiente sent a snake here.

212
00:14:45,801 --> 00:14:48,762
So the Ardientes are trying
to scare us again?

213
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:52,433
<i>Do they really think</i>
<i>their antics will frighten us?</i>

214
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,393
They're just fueling our courage.

215
00:14:54,935 --> 00:14:56,103
Just be careful, Auntie.

216
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:57,646
I will, Diego.

217
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:06,363
Next, please.

218
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:11,577
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

219
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:17,041
I'd just like to ask for
records of the Women's Union.

220
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:19,376
The group has long been abolished, ma'am.

221
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:20,836
It's for research purposes.

222
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:24,590
I'll use it as a prototype
for further studies.

223
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,467
I plan to pursue a master's degree.

224
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,427
-Mm. Just a minute.
-Thank you.

225
00:15:36,685 --> 00:15:37,937
[woman] Hello, ma'am Eds.

226
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:41,106
Someone here is asking
about the Women's Union.

227
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:43,317
Do you know where our files are?

228
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:52,701
Uh… Okay, ma'am. Thank you.

229
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:58,290
Ma'am, I'm sorry but we have no records.

230
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:02,127
None? No records? What do you mean?

231
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:04,755
I'm asking for public documents.

232
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:06,840
We have none.

233
00:16:06,924 --> 00:16:09,176
Just come back when my boss is available.

234
00:16:09,259 --> 00:16:10,219
She's on leave.

235
00:16:27,861 --> 00:16:29,071
[woman] Next, please.

236
00:16:38,455 --> 00:16:41,291
Here. Keep the change, man.

237
00:16:41,792 --> 00:16:43,377
Because when I exit that door,

238
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:45,337
I'd be luckier than a lottery winner.

239
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:47,589
Thank you.

240
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:05,274
[unsettling music playing]

241
00:17:13,782 --> 00:17:16,035
[inner voice] <i>What are</i>
<i>you waiting for? Fire it.</i>

242
00:17:17,077 --> 00:17:18,787
<i>Come on. Fire it.</i>

243
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:22,916
<i>Fire it. You're useless, Arnaldo.</i>

244
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:25,419
<i>Besides, you're a murderer.</i>

245
00:17:25,794 --> 00:17:30,716
<i>You killed Carlotta, Nimfa,</i>
<i>and other innocent people.</i>

246
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:35,137
<i>All for the love of a woman</i>
<i>you will never have</i>

247
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:36,722
<i>because she's lying to you.</i>

248
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:40,267
<i>You're an idiot, Arnaldo. You're stupid.</i>

249
00:17:40,684 --> 00:17:43,437
<i>A moron! Kill yourself! Do it!</i>

250
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,065
-Ah…
-Who are you?

251
00:17:46,148 --> 00:17:48,358
Good afternoon. I'm Jerry Dimalanta.

252
00:17:48,442 --> 00:17:49,902
Can I talk to the mayor?

253
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:51,779
You again? Ivy, this man…

254
00:17:52,237 --> 00:17:56,950
Why are you following me?
Don't you dare touch me again!

255
00:17:57,493 --> 00:18:00,120
How did you find me here?
I have many bodyguards.

256
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:02,706
Emilia, relax. How can I help you?

257
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,500
I just want to talk to the mayor.

258
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:07,503
He needs to know what I know.

259
00:18:07,795 --> 00:18:09,213
You have to trust me.

260
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:13,258
If you let me talk to him,
I'm sure you won't regret it.

261
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:20,182
Especially not the mayor.

262
00:18:20,265 --> 00:18:24,311
[tense music playing]

263
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:35,197
No! No!

264
00:18:41,078 --> 00:18:42,037
[groans]

265
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:43,080
[knocks on door]

266
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:44,206
Arnaldo.

267
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:47,209
Arnaldo.

268
00:18:48,293 --> 00:18:49,586
Hey, open the door.

269
00:18:51,046 --> 00:18:52,381
[knocking continues]

270
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:54,508
-This isn't over.
-Son, somebody wants to see you.

271
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:02,516
This isn't over.

272
00:19:21,535 --> 00:19:24,830
Emilia, where did you meet Mr. Jerry?

273
00:19:25,539 --> 00:19:27,624
He might be a spy for Diego.

274
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:30,252
Oh, Ivy, just don't mind him.

275
00:19:30,335 --> 00:19:31,587
He must be a fanatic.

276
00:19:32,379 --> 00:19:34,131
Anyway, how are you and Arnaldo?

277
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:37,134
Well, please tell the congressman

278
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:38,051
that he's getting worse.

279
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:40,345
We need to re-admit him to the psych ward.

280
00:19:40,929 --> 00:19:44,016
I know you came here
to keep an eye on things

281
00:19:44,099 --> 00:19:45,893
and report to the congressman.

282
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:49,605
So, tell him that.
Or, I have a better idea.

283
00:19:49,855 --> 00:19:54,193
What if you stay here so we can
both take care of Arnaldo?

284
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:56,069
-What do you think?
-Oh.

285
00:19:56,862 --> 00:20:00,699
Ivy, can we skip
the depressing topics for later?

286
00:20:00,949 --> 00:20:03,577
You know, I came here
not just for Arnaldo.

287
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:07,414
I came here to talk to you
regarding my candidacy

288
00:20:07,497 --> 00:20:10,751
because you still haven't
given me any straight answer.

289
00:20:10,834 --> 00:20:12,252
So, will you support me or not?

290
00:20:13,295 --> 00:20:15,380
Doesn't this annoy you?

291
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:19,551
You always want to talk
about your political career

292
00:20:19,635 --> 00:20:21,178
whenever you visit me.

293
00:20:22,721 --> 00:20:24,890
[sighs] You're lucky I'm a patient woman.

294
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:28,685
Fine. Let's talk about it,
but before that…

295
00:20:30,687 --> 00:20:33,607
I need to know everything, Emilia.

296
00:20:34,858 --> 00:20:38,403
All the good and not-so-good
things you did before.

297
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:43,033
I want to know all your secrets.

298
00:20:44,409 --> 00:20:50,165
Because from there,
I'll know how to stand for you,

299
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:53,418
how to support you,
and how to protect you.

300
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,965
Do you remember
what you told me at the bar?

301
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:03,553
About billions. Remember?

302
00:21:05,389 --> 00:21:06,890
I--I said that?

303
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:10,352
-Really? I did?
-Yes.

304
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:14,815
[chuckles]

305
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:17,192
Me and my big mouth, honestly.

306
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:18,860
When I drink, that's my problem.

307
00:21:18,944 --> 00:21:20,737
That's always been my problem, Ivy.

308
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:23,198
-So, is it true?
-I spill too much…

309
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:24,908
-when I'm drunk.
-Is it true, Emilia?

310
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:27,369
[sighs] Okay, okay.

311
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:29,079
I must admit…

312
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:33,583
yeah, that was during my time as mayor.

313
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:37,379
Um, I'd get commissions.
But that was before.

314
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:39,840
-Before.
-[phone rings]

315
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:42,384
Wait, I just have an important call.

316
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:43,802
Hello?

317
00:21:45,804 --> 00:21:46,847
[Emilia] Yes?

318
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:53,395
[phone rings]

319
00:21:55,897 --> 00:21:56,898
[phone rings]

320
00:21:58,358 --> 00:21:59,359
<i>Mom?</i>

321
00:22:00,110 --> 00:22:01,653
I didn't get any information here…

322
00:22:01,737 --> 00:22:02,863
<i>at the city hall.</i>

323
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:05,032
<i>But I'm sure of one thing.</i>

324
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:07,409
The Ardientes are hiding something

325
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:09,286
in the group Emilia established.

326
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:12,706
Mom, Emilia just told me
something that matches up…

327
00:22:13,081 --> 00:22:14,958
<i>with the information you're getting.</i>

328
00:22:16,335 --> 00:22:19,755
<i>She's possibly getting her stolen funds…</i>

329
00:22:19,838 --> 00:22:21,631
through that commission.

330
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:26,720
Don't worry.
I won't stop investigating this.

331
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:30,390
I'll find out what they're hiding.

332
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:32,726
Okay, Mom.

333
00:22:33,935 --> 00:22:39,149
[tense music playing]

334
00:22:49,576 --> 00:22:50,660
[Jerry] Oh, Mayor.

335
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:54,414
Hurry up, I don't have time.

336
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:56,917
I'm sure you won't regret this, Mayor.

337
00:22:57,584 --> 00:22:58,543
You're wasting my time.

338
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:02,380
Relax, Mayor!
I don't need anything from you.

339
00:23:03,048 --> 00:23:04,883
Truth is, you're the one who needs me.

340
00:23:05,717 --> 00:23:08,845
And I'm sure you'll give me a lot of money

341
00:23:08,929 --> 00:23:10,222
for what I'm going to give you.

342
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:16,394
[unsettling music playing]

343
00:23:22,901 --> 00:23:23,944
A broken cell phone?

344
00:23:24,778 --> 00:23:26,404
What am I supposed to do with this thing?

345
00:23:26,488 --> 00:23:27,447
Smash it on your head?

346
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:28,698
Mayor. Mayor.

347
00:23:29,366 --> 00:23:31,159
First, ask what exactly
is in that cellphone.

348
00:23:35,372 --> 00:23:38,917
This contains the dark truth
about your beloved Ivy.

349
00:23:42,921 --> 00:23:46,341
[upbeat music playing]

350
00:23:57,894 --> 00:23:59,521
[Nimfa] <i>I'm sure about this, ma'am Emilia.</i>

351
00:23:59,604 --> 00:24:01,815
<i>I'll find out just who she is.</i>

352
00:24:02,357 --> 00:24:05,318
[Emilia] <i>Take a video, and</i>
<i>send it to me immediately.</i>

353
00:24:06,069 --> 00:24:07,237
<i>Pick up, Emilia.</i>

354
00:24:07,946 --> 00:24:09,948
<i>Ma'am Emilia… I know the truth!</i>

355
00:24:10,031 --> 00:24:11,700
<i>-Ivy Aguas and Lily--</i>
<i>-No!</i>

356
00:24:15,453 --> 00:24:16,788
<i>Mayor Arnaldo! Mayor…</i>

357
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:19,207
<i>-You need to know that Ivy is---</i>
<i>-That's not true!</i>

358
00:24:20,834 --> 00:24:21,835
[Fernan] <i>Nimfa!</i>

359
00:24:22,252 --> 00:24:23,795
<i>-Mister Fernan!</i>
<i>-Nimfa!</i>

360
00:24:24,838 --> 00:24:26,006
<i>This is Nimfa's cellphone.</i>

361
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:29,759
<i>You'll find Nimfa and Emilia's</i>
<i>text message exchanges there.</i>

362
00:24:30,510 --> 00:24:33,555
[tense music playing]

363
00:24:34,931 --> 00:24:36,391
[breathing deeply]

364
00:24:51,531 --> 00:24:54,618
[tense music playing]

365
00:25:23,396 --> 00:25:25,899
<i>Mayor Ardiente needs to see this.</i>

366
00:25:30,362 --> 00:25:32,906
Mayor, just watch the video.
To see is to believe!

367
00:25:41,748 --> 00:25:44,751
[tense music continues playing]

368
00:25:51,841 --> 00:25:52,884
[Emilia] Ivy!

369
00:25:54,135 --> 00:25:56,596
Ivy, I hate to say this, but I have to go.

370
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,306
I have an emergency.

371
00:25:58,390 --> 00:26:00,517
Emergency? What happened? Are you okay?

372
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:03,228
Well, let's just say a little bird told me

373
00:26:03,311 --> 00:26:07,190
that somebody is snooping
in my old playground.

374
00:26:08,608 --> 00:26:11,069
Well, at least, you know it isn't me.

375
00:26:11,987 --> 00:26:13,738
I'll tell you more about it tomorrow.

376
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:16,741
Tell Arnaldo I left already. Bye-bye.

377
00:26:16,825 --> 00:26:18,702
-Take care.
-Thank you.

378
00:26:25,208 --> 00:26:27,752
<i>-Mom.</i>
<i>-Lily, dear.</i>

379
00:26:28,545 --> 00:26:31,423
[Ivy] <i>I'm sorry that I had</i>
<i>to point a gun at you earlier.</i>

380
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:35,552
[Camia] <i>It's all right, Lily.</i>
<i>I understand why.</i>

381
00:26:39,389 --> 00:26:40,724
Ivy is Lily?

382
00:26:42,976 --> 00:26:44,436
Ivy and Lily are one?

383
00:26:47,647 --> 00:26:49,316
They're the same person?

384
00:26:50,650 --> 00:26:53,528
[Ivy] <i>Mr. Mayor? My name is Ivy.</i>

385
00:26:54,487 --> 00:26:55,905
<i>Ivy Aguas.</i>

386
00:27:00,035 --> 00:27:03,121
[Arnaldo sighs] <i>You really are</i>
<i>something else, Miss Aguas.</i>

387
00:27:03,413 --> 00:27:06,249
<i>Thank you for investing</i>
<i>in our project, by the way.</i>

388
00:27:07,083 --> 00:27:12,714
<i>I invested a lot, Mr. Mayor.</i>
<i>I'll expect a lot in return.</i>

389
00:27:15,216 --> 00:27:17,552
[Arnaldo] <i>I want to be a senator.</i>
<i>I need your help.</i>

390
00:27:17,927 --> 00:27:20,972
[Ivy] <i>The farmer's lands. Give it to me.</i>

391
00:27:23,641 --> 00:27:26,478
[Arnaldo] <i>Are you doing this</i>
<i>for the farmers or for Diego?</i>

392
00:27:27,270 --> 00:27:29,564
<i>Well, Mr. Mayor, it's not my fault</i>

393
00:27:29,647 --> 00:27:33,526
<i>your brother moves faster… than you do.</i>

394
00:27:35,904 --> 00:27:37,030
All this time?

395
00:27:38,073 --> 00:27:40,075
[Ivy] <i>Diego and I still see each other.</i>

396
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:41,910
<i>But I told him to stay away.</i>

397
00:27:41,993 --> 00:27:44,996
<i>Because I know I'm sure</i>
<i>of my feelings for you.</i>

398
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:48,208
<i>Arnaldo, I'm not playing you. I love you.</i>

399
00:27:48,583 --> 00:27:50,293
<i>I love you, Arnaldo.</i>

400
00:27:50,585 --> 00:27:52,712
[Julio] <i>I couldn't help but notice…</i>

401
00:27:52,796 --> 00:27:56,716
<i>you and Miss Aguas are growing closer.</i>

402
00:27:57,092 --> 00:28:00,428
<i>It seems like you're drunk</i>
<i>on love, or should I say lust?</i>

403
00:28:01,179 --> 00:28:03,306
<i>Don't be stupid.</i>

404
00:28:03,390 --> 00:28:06,476
<i>Because of your actions, you're</i>
<i>starting to look like a fool.</i>

405
00:28:06,851 --> 00:28:09,312
[Arnaldo] <i>A lifetime of love</i>
<i>and happiness… with me.</i>

406
00:28:09,396 --> 00:28:12,315
<i>Ivy Aguas, I love you. Will you marry me?</i>

407
00:28:12,857 --> 00:28:14,109
<i>Yes, Arnaldo!</i>

408
00:28:14,776 --> 00:28:16,694
All this time, she's been lying to me?

409
00:28:16,945 --> 00:28:19,489
[Arnaldo] <i>You know, sometimes I</i>
<i>think you're just leading me on.</i>

410
00:28:19,572 --> 00:28:21,574
<i>One minute, you're hot,</i>
<i>the next thing, you're cold.</i>

411
00:28:21,658 --> 00:28:22,700
<i>What do you really want?</i>

412
00:28:22,784 --> 00:28:24,994
[Julio] <i>Arnaldo, I have a suspicion</i>

413
00:28:25,078 --> 00:28:27,705
<i>that Miss Aguas is hiding something.</i>

414
00:28:27,789 --> 00:28:30,375
<i>Damn it, Madrigal!</i>
<i>I told you not to lose her.</i>

415
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:32,877
<i>Mayor, I'm sorry. It was my mistake.</i>

416
00:28:32,961 --> 00:28:34,212
<i>Did you do it intentionally?</i>

417
00:28:34,295 --> 00:28:35,797
<i>What are you doing here, Madrigal?</i>

418
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:38,174
<i>I called your number one man over</i>

419
00:28:38,258 --> 00:28:41,553
<i>to ask what kind of gift you might like</i>

420
00:28:41,636 --> 00:28:43,430
<i>because your birthday's coming up soon.</i>

421
00:28:43,513 --> 00:28:45,765
<i>Grandpa, Mom, you have to see this.</i>

422
00:28:46,474 --> 00:28:47,600
<i>Madrigal?</i>

423
00:28:48,017 --> 00:28:50,645
[Julio] <i>We finally caught the rat.</i>

424
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:53,064
<i>Kill Madrigal in front of us</i>

425
00:28:53,148 --> 00:28:55,984
<i>to prove that we're no different.</i>

426
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:56,943
[groans]

427
00:28:57,444 --> 00:29:01,322
[Ivy] <i>I won't taint my hands</i>
<i>just to prove my loyalty!</i>

428
00:29:02,157 --> 00:29:03,700
Everything I did for her.

429
00:29:03,783 --> 00:29:06,828
All this time, she's using me?
She's using me?!

430
00:29:07,454 --> 00:29:08,496
She's using me.

431
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:10,373
<i>Lily Cruz is alive, Aunt Claire.</i>

432
00:29:10,457 --> 00:29:13,960
<i>She's Camia's backer. She's alive.</i>

433
00:29:14,043 --> 00:29:16,421
[Claire] <i>Lily Cruz? Camia's daughter?</i>

434
00:29:16,504 --> 00:29:18,840
[Arnaldo] <i>You know what's funny?</i>
<i>Mama mentioned that…</i>

435
00:29:18,923 --> 00:29:21,384
<i>because you didn't tell us</i>
<i>you were adopted,</i>

436
00:29:21,468 --> 00:29:26,473
<i>there's a possibility that</i>
<i>you could be Lily Cruz.</i>

437
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:29,350
<i>This Lily Cruz is the one backing up…</i>

438
00:29:29,434 --> 00:29:31,019
<i>-Camia and Diego.</i>
<i>-Arnaldo!</i>

439
00:29:31,102 --> 00:29:34,147
[Ivy] <i>What you saw was the</i>
<i>only thing we were doing.</i>

440
00:29:34,230 --> 00:29:35,565
[Arnaldo] <i>What were you talking about?</i>

441
00:29:35,648 --> 00:29:38,151
<i>How the two of you</i>
<i>will stab me behind my back?</i>

442
00:29:38,234 --> 00:29:42,822
[Ivy] <i>If you don't believe me,</i>
<i>if you think I'm betraying you,</i>

443
00:29:42,906 --> 00:29:44,157
<i>let's just stop this.</i>

444
00:29:44,574 --> 00:29:46,659
<i>We should call off our wedding.</i>

445
00:29:51,664 --> 00:29:54,417
[Nimfa] <i>She's the one feeding</i>
<i>information to Diego's camp.</i>

446
00:29:54,501 --> 00:29:56,920
<i>-That's not true!</i>
<i>-She's Diego's spy…</i>

447
00:29:57,003 --> 00:29:59,297
<i>-That's not true!</i>
<i>-…within the Ardiente family!</i>

448
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:00,632
<i>She's just using you.</i>

449
00:30:00,715 --> 00:30:02,967
<i>-That's not true!</i>
<i>-Mayor, you need to know…</i>

450
00:30:03,051 --> 00:30:04,677
<i>-that Ivy is--</i>
<i>-That's not true!</i>

451
00:30:04,928 --> 00:30:09,390
<i>You need to believe me,</i>
<i>Arnaldo, not that farmhand.</i>

452
00:30:09,474 --> 00:30:11,768
<i>If you believe me, we'll get married.</i>

453
00:30:12,018 --> 00:30:14,312
<i>I believe you. I believe</i>
<i>everything that you say!</i>

454
00:30:14,854 --> 00:30:16,439
[Ivy] <i>That's all I need.</i>

455
00:30:16,898 --> 00:30:18,900
<i>We'll push through with the wedding.</i>

456
00:30:21,319 --> 00:30:24,113
<i>-I've got Ivy Aguas.</i>
<i>-Well, I have you now!</i>

457
00:30:24,906 --> 00:30:26,074
<i>I can easily kill you</i>

458
00:30:26,157 --> 00:30:28,201
<i>and make it look</i>
<i>like you committed suicide,</i>

459
00:30:28,701 --> 00:30:30,245
<i>just like what I did to Carlotta.</i>

460
00:30:30,537 --> 00:30:31,955
<i>Monster!</i>

461
00:30:32,038 --> 00:30:35,416
<i>-I didn't mean to!</i>
<i>-You monster! I don't love you!</i>

462
00:30:35,917 --> 00:30:38,002
<i>I'll never love a demon like you!</i>

463
00:30:38,294 --> 00:30:39,504
<i>You're a demon!</i>

464
00:30:39,587 --> 00:30:41,631
<i>-You love me.</i>
<i>-I don't love you!</i>

465
00:30:41,714 --> 00:30:42,841
<i>You love me.</i>

466
00:30:42,924 --> 00:30:45,009
<i>Arrest this man! Take him to prison!</i>

467
00:30:45,552 --> 00:30:47,387
<i>Arrest Arnaldo!</i>

468
00:30:47,470 --> 00:30:50,807
[Julio] <i>Stop them! I said, stop them!</i>

469
00:30:50,890 --> 00:30:52,809
[tense music intensifies]

470
00:30:52,892 --> 00:31:00,024
She used me. She used me…
Damn. That bitch.

471
00:31:06,406 --> 00:31:08,283
That bitch. That bitch.

472
00:31:08,908 --> 00:31:12,871
That bitch. She used me.

473
00:31:14,831 --> 00:31:18,084
Mayor, you look like
you're about to kill someone.

474
00:31:18,835 --> 00:31:19,836
Mayor!

475
00:31:24,632 --> 00:31:26,676
[grunts]

476
00:31:27,802 --> 00:31:31,472
[grunts]

477
00:31:39,105 --> 00:31:42,108
[dark music playing]

478
00:31:50,700 --> 00:31:53,661
We've succeeded in refiling
the case in the new RTC branch

479
00:31:53,745 --> 00:31:54,746
here in Ardiente.

480
00:31:55,496 --> 00:31:56,956
Contrary to popular belief,

481
00:31:57,248 --> 00:31:59,876
not all RTC branches
are controlled by the Ardientes.

482
00:31:59,959 --> 00:32:01,586
This one particular judge

483
00:32:01,669 --> 00:32:03,713
is connected to the Court of Appeals

484
00:32:03,796 --> 00:32:05,715
and is a well-known
critic of the Ardientes.

485
00:32:07,008 --> 00:32:08,760
I'll just update you about the case.

486
00:32:09,928 --> 00:32:11,012
Listen, everyone.

487
00:32:11,638 --> 00:32:13,556
Our fight continues.

488
00:32:13,640 --> 00:32:15,141
We shouldn't be afraid of the Ardientes,

489
00:32:15,224 --> 00:32:17,810
and no one will back out of the campaign.

490
00:32:18,102 --> 00:32:20,438
-[all] That's right!
-For a new Ardiente!

491
00:32:20,521 --> 00:32:22,190
[all] For a new Ardiente!

492
00:32:22,273 --> 00:32:25,068
[clapping]

493
00:32:28,696 --> 00:32:29,697
[Julio] Sanggano.

494
00:32:30,156 --> 00:32:35,912
What was Diego Torillo's
reaction to the gift I sent him?

495
00:32:36,496 --> 00:32:38,081
He was frightened, Congressman.

496
00:32:38,164 --> 00:32:38,998
[laughs]

497
00:32:39,082 --> 00:32:43,044
Their uninvited guest caused a
commotion at their headquarters.

498
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:46,965
-Sir!
-Where's Emilia?

499
00:32:47,298 --> 00:32:50,218
-Ma'am Emilia told us not to let you in.
-I need to talk to her.

500
00:32:50,301 --> 00:32:51,636
Let me in! Let me in.

501
00:32:51,719 --> 00:32:54,889
-Sir, she's not here.
-I said let me in!

502
00:32:54,973 --> 00:32:57,600
-I told you, she's not here!
-What did you say?

503
00:32:58,017 --> 00:33:00,353
-She's not here.
-Let me go.

504
00:33:00,436 --> 00:33:02,563
-Sir, please.
-Step aside!

505
00:33:02,814 --> 00:33:07,068
Diego Torillo's group
is campaigning today, right?

506
00:33:08,528 --> 00:33:12,865
You know, I have been very,
very patient with them,

507
00:33:12,949 --> 00:33:14,867
which is actually a very rare thing.

508
00:33:15,535 --> 00:33:18,287
I could've just stomped on him
and crushed him…

509
00:33:19,914 --> 00:33:21,374
like dust.

510
00:33:21,916 --> 00:33:24,127
I think you're getting soft, Congressman.

511
00:33:24,961 --> 00:33:27,005
Maybe you can say that.

512
00:33:27,922 --> 00:33:28,965
Perhaps…

513
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:33,970
I think I was really affected
by what happened to Arnaldo.

514
00:33:35,096 --> 00:33:40,852
But I am done trying to be good and decent

515
00:33:40,935 --> 00:33:43,104
about this whole fiasco.

516
00:33:45,773 --> 00:33:48,484
I want you to bring me Diego Torillo.

517
00:33:49,277 --> 00:33:50,445
Any which way.

518
00:33:52,030 --> 00:33:55,616
Dead or alive, it doesn't matter.

519
00:33:57,869 --> 00:33:58,995
Yes, sir.

520
00:34:12,842 --> 00:34:13,926
Good morning.

521
00:34:14,469 --> 00:34:15,678
Good morning.

522
00:34:17,096 --> 00:34:18,139
What's our schedule for today?

523
00:34:20,558 --> 00:34:24,520
Well, Dr. Go is coming today
for your checkup.

524
00:34:25,438 --> 00:34:26,397
Cancel that.

525
00:34:28,149 --> 00:34:29,275
There's no need for one.

526
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:32,695
For some reason, I feel good.

527
00:34:33,613 --> 00:34:35,948
No, actually, I feel really good.

528
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:38,201
I don't know why.

529
00:34:38,534 --> 00:34:40,912
I haven't felt this good in months.

530
00:34:46,793 --> 00:34:51,047
Good. I'll call your mom
to tell her we're going home.

531
00:34:51,130 --> 00:34:52,799
No, no, no, no. Not so fast.

532
00:34:54,509 --> 00:34:57,261
Why don't we stay here first
and enjoy the rest house?

533
00:34:58,387 --> 00:35:01,599
You know, make the most of our lives

534
00:35:01,682 --> 00:35:03,976
before returning to Poblacion Ardiente.

535
00:35:05,269 --> 00:35:06,395
Let's go home tomorrow.

536
00:35:07,396 --> 00:35:11,567
Give me this one more day
with you, and I promise…

537
00:35:13,152 --> 00:35:14,362
we'll have so much fun.

538
00:35:16,781 --> 00:35:17,990
How does that sound?

539
00:35:20,910 --> 00:35:22,703
Great! Let's eat.

540
00:35:24,288 --> 00:35:26,415
<i>Are you acting like this</i>
<i>because you're sick</i>

541
00:35:26,499 --> 00:35:28,751
<i>or because you're playing tricks on me?</i>

542
00:35:29,460 --> 00:35:34,215
<i>I'll find out what's going on</i>
<i>in your mind, Arnaldo.</i>

543
00:35:40,054 --> 00:35:41,222
[Diego] Get this printed as well.

544
00:35:41,305 --> 00:35:42,598
[man] Here are the remaining posters.

545
00:35:42,682 --> 00:35:43,850
[Diego] Okay, put it over there.

546
00:35:50,898 --> 00:35:53,484
[indistinct chatter]

547
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:56,070
Excuse me.

548
00:36:10,459 --> 00:36:11,460
Son.

549
00:36:12,128 --> 00:36:13,129
Dad.

550
00:36:18,092 --> 00:36:19,135
How are you?

551
00:36:20,970 --> 00:36:22,847
I'm okay, Dad. How are you?

552
00:36:23,431 --> 00:36:27,894
Well… I have something
important I want to tell you.

553
00:36:29,770 --> 00:36:31,564
It's about your campaign for later.

554
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:35,109
I don't think you should go.

555
00:36:36,736 --> 00:36:39,071
Julio's planning something
against you, and it's not good.

556
00:36:39,780 --> 00:36:42,909
He's going to kidnap you
and kill you, son.

557
00:36:43,284 --> 00:36:45,870
Julio's already attempted
to kill me several times.

558
00:36:46,662 --> 00:36:48,080
I can take care of myself, Dad.

559
00:36:48,915 --> 00:36:50,499
I know you can, son.

560
00:36:51,375 --> 00:36:52,668
But what about your supporters?

561
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:54,754
Can you stand to see them getting hurt?

562
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:57,423
And getting hurt is just one
thing, what if they get killed?

563
00:36:58,257 --> 00:37:01,344
You won't always be able
to protect yourself.

564
00:37:01,427 --> 00:37:05,014
You need allies, someone on your side.

565
00:37:05,473 --> 00:37:08,726
You need the protection
of strong people, like Jaguar.

566
00:37:09,352 --> 00:37:12,730
But, Dad, that man is a criminal.

567
00:37:13,481 --> 00:37:14,482
[scoffs]

568
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:18,069
Well, whatever he is,

569
00:37:18,152 --> 00:37:20,238
what's important is you're
fighting for the same things.

570
00:37:20,321 --> 00:37:22,573
He wants to bring down the Ardientes too.

571
00:37:22,990 --> 00:37:25,910
If that happens, if he protects you,

572
00:37:26,452 --> 00:37:28,120
you'll be ruling over Ardiente--

573
00:37:28,204 --> 00:37:29,288
Hang on, Dad…

574
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:31,666
Do you know Jaguar?

575
00:37:32,416 --> 00:37:33,876
Why do you want me to side with him?

576
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:35,711
Are you working together?

577
00:37:37,588 --> 00:37:38,756
Dad, no matter what happens,

578
00:37:38,839 --> 00:37:40,925
I won't align myself with Jaguar.

579
00:37:41,384 --> 00:37:44,220
I'll protect my supporters

580
00:37:44,303 --> 00:37:46,055
without gripping the edge of a knife.

581
00:37:46,722 --> 00:37:49,725
[tense music playing]

582
00:38:10,204 --> 00:38:11,122
Hon.

583
00:38:12,206 --> 00:38:15,209
[tense music playing]

584
00:38:33,436 --> 00:38:36,522
[tense music playing]

585
00:38:59,795 --> 00:39:01,130
Come on. Swim.

586
00:39:08,179 --> 00:39:11,265
[tense music playing]

587
00:39:26,655 --> 00:39:28,741
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

588
00:39:29,784 --> 00:39:30,868
Can I ask you something?

589
00:39:32,328 --> 00:39:33,329
Why do you love me?

590
00:39:33,913 --> 00:39:35,581
I can't answer that.

591
00:39:39,043 --> 00:39:40,711
As other people have put it,

592
00:39:41,545 --> 00:39:46,509
there's no right or wrong reason
why you love somebody.

593
00:39:47,343 --> 00:39:49,136
It's my turn to ask you something.

594
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:51,347
Sure.

595
00:39:52,348 --> 00:39:54,475
How was your talk with Mister Jerry?

596
00:39:55,476 --> 00:39:58,437
-Mr. Jerry?
-What did you talk about?

597
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:03,192
Well, we had an interesting
conversation, and then he left.

598
00:40:04,777 --> 00:40:07,238
I didn't see him leave, Arnaldo.

599
00:40:07,321 --> 00:40:09,573
Well, that is because you were with Mom.

600
00:40:11,283 --> 00:40:13,160
You know what, Ivy?
Let's not talk about it.

601
00:40:13,661 --> 00:40:14,662
Sit down.

602
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:18,958
Let's focus on the now.

603
00:40:20,209 --> 00:40:21,585
Here, with me.

604
00:40:23,087 --> 00:40:24,839
The present is so delicate

605
00:40:24,922 --> 00:40:27,591
that we don't know
what tomorrow will bring.

606
00:40:29,009 --> 00:40:31,470
But you know, I've been thinking…

607
00:40:32,513 --> 00:40:34,598
if I die today…

608
00:40:37,560 --> 00:40:38,561
I'll have it.

609
00:40:40,354 --> 00:40:41,730
I'd rather die with you.

610
00:40:44,150 --> 00:40:45,609
And I'll be fine with it.

611
00:40:48,571 --> 00:40:49,780
I love you.

612
00:40:55,786 --> 00:41:00,749
I really, really love you.

613
00:41:01,375 --> 00:41:04,462
[tense music playing]

614
00:41:17,475 --> 00:41:20,436
[suspenseful music playing]

615
00:41:29,487 --> 00:41:32,490
[suspenseful music continues]

616
00:42:05,356 --> 00:42:07,483
-What are you doing here?
-Arnaldo.

617
00:42:07,942 --> 00:42:08,943
Well…

618
00:42:10,027 --> 00:42:11,028
[Ivy scoffs]

619
00:42:20,579 --> 00:42:21,789
I was waiting for you.

620
00:42:33,217 --> 00:42:34,885
Ivy. Let's go.

621
00:42:35,970 --> 00:42:37,054
-What?
-Let's go.

622
00:42:37,137 --> 00:42:38,180
Don't you want to?

623
00:42:38,931 --> 00:42:41,976
I'd love to, but we have
to do something first.

624
00:42:42,059 --> 00:42:43,018
Get dressed.

625
00:42:44,937 --> 00:42:45,896
Okay? Go.

626
00:42:45,980 --> 00:42:46,814
-Okay.
-Get dressed.

627
00:42:46,897 --> 00:42:48,899
-Ouch!
-We'll go somewhere.

628
00:43:05,583 --> 00:43:08,294
<i>I'll discover what you're hiding.</i>

629
00:43:08,669 --> 00:43:13,090
<i>And once I do, I'll finish you off myself.</i>

630
00:43:21,640 --> 00:43:23,642
[indistinct chatter]

631
00:43:25,144 --> 00:43:26,478
[woman] My goodness! It stinks!

632
00:43:27,438 --> 00:43:28,897
I'll call the authorities!

633
00:43:28,981 --> 00:43:30,858
-What's happening?
-There's a dead body.

634
00:43:30,941 --> 00:43:32,776
[eerie music]

635
00:43:36,530 --> 00:43:39,491
[unsettling music playing]

636
00:43:49,585 --> 00:43:52,546
[Arnaldo] <i>What are you</i>
<i>talking about? Revenge?</i>

637
00:43:54,048 --> 00:43:56,592
<i>You don't know a thing! You don't!</i>

638
00:43:57,384 --> 00:43:58,510
<i>You have no proof.</i>

639
00:43:58,594 --> 00:44:01,889
<i>Unless you can prove everything</i>
<i>you're accusing Ivy of,</i>

640
00:44:01,972 --> 00:44:03,223
<i>I won't believe you.</i>

641
00:44:03,891 --> 00:44:05,684
<i>How was your talk with Mister Jerry?</i>

642
00:44:06,226 --> 00:44:09,897
<i>Well, we had an interesting</i>
<i>conversation, and then he left.</i>

643
00:44:11,106 --> 00:44:14,151
[unsettling music playing]

644
00:44:22,242 --> 00:44:25,287
[tense music playing]

645
00:44:40,260 --> 00:44:42,429
[tense music continues playing]

646
00:44:49,978 --> 00:44:52,564
[tense music intensifies]

647
00:44:58,779 --> 00:44:59,863
<i>Mom.</i>

648
00:44:59,947 --> 00:45:01,323
<i>Lily, dear.</i>

649
00:45:10,916 --> 00:45:14,294
[ominous music playing]

650
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:38,235
[line rings]

651
00:45:38,318 --> 00:45:42,906
It is an honor for me and
for my colleagues to serve you.

652
00:45:43,824 --> 00:45:46,994
Our aim is to give happiness

653
00:45:47,077 --> 00:45:50,622
and hope to our constituents
here in this home for the aged.

654
00:45:51,039 --> 00:45:54,543
I highly respect you,
grandfathers and grandmothers.

655
00:45:57,212 --> 00:45:58,839
Diego, pick up.

656
00:46:01,467 --> 00:46:04,094
We have a few things to give you.

657
00:46:04,761 --> 00:46:05,971
And we hope you like them.

658
00:46:06,555 --> 00:46:09,558
[applause]

659
00:46:17,441 --> 00:46:19,193
Why did you throw it there?

660
00:46:19,818 --> 00:46:21,111
Did I tell you to throw it there?

661
00:46:21,820 --> 00:46:24,490
Get that body, clean it,

662
00:46:25,199 --> 00:46:27,201
and take it somewhere else. Okay?

663
00:46:27,284 --> 00:46:29,703
Because if you don't,
your body will lie in its place.

664
00:46:29,786 --> 00:46:31,622
-Do you understand?
-Yes, Mayor.

665
00:46:31,997 --> 00:46:34,249
-Go. Go! Now!
-Yes.

666
00:46:45,219 --> 00:46:49,556
[line ringing]

667
00:46:50,557 --> 00:46:51,600
Arnaldo.

668
00:46:54,102 --> 00:46:57,022
Where've you been?
I've been looking for you.

669
00:47:00,567 --> 00:47:02,402
I just asked the bodyguards
to check the car.

670
00:47:06,156 --> 00:47:07,157
Okay.

671
00:47:10,244 --> 00:47:12,996
You know what? Um… I was thinking.

672
00:47:13,539 --> 00:47:19,169
What if… we go to the place
we're supposed to go to alone?

673
00:47:19,586 --> 00:47:21,880
No bodyguards. What do you think?

674
00:47:25,133 --> 00:47:28,095
I like it. Good idea.

675
00:47:32,140 --> 00:47:36,770
So, where are you taking me?

676
00:47:38,105 --> 00:47:39,147
I can't tell you.

677
00:47:39,565 --> 00:47:40,816
It's a surprise.

678
00:47:41,900 --> 00:47:44,027
But, I promise you, you'll have fun.

679
00:47:46,280 --> 00:47:49,408
Exciting. Okay. You go ahead.

680
00:47:50,158 --> 00:47:51,451
I'll just get my things.

681
00:47:52,077 --> 00:47:55,372
Okay. I'll meet you outside.
I'll go get something too.

682
00:47:57,749 --> 00:48:00,836
[tense music playing]

683
00:48:26,653 --> 00:48:28,196
Damn you, Arnaldo.

684
00:48:29,740 --> 00:48:33,952
I'll kill you before
you find out who I really am.

685
00:48:34,661 --> 00:48:37,789
[tense music playing]

686
00:48:53,597 --> 00:48:57,976
I'll make you pay for lying to me,

687
00:48:58,894 --> 00:49:00,354
Ivy Aguas.

688
00:49:03,899 --> 00:49:04,983
But, before that…

689
00:49:07,527 --> 00:49:08,987
you'll make me happy.

690
00:49:18,121 --> 00:49:22,334
<i>I'm jealous of your</i>
<i>close friendship with this…</i>

691
00:49:22,417 --> 00:49:23,710
<i>Lily Cruz.</i>

692
00:49:23,794 --> 00:49:26,380
<i>I'm not talking about</i>
<i>the Lily Cruz that you're with.</i>

693
00:49:26,463 --> 00:49:29,383
<i>She's an impostor. That's right.</i>

694
00:49:29,466 --> 00:49:32,344
<i>I'm going to make her regret</i>
<i>all the things that she did to me,</i>

695
00:49:32,427 --> 00:49:33,345
<i>and then, I'll kill her.</i>

696
00:49:33,428 --> 00:49:35,764
<i>There's a bomb, everyone! There's a bomb!</i>

697
00:49:35,847 --> 00:49:36,973
[laughs]

698
00:49:37,057 --> 00:49:39,685
<i>We're the only ones here,</i>
<i>so you can do whatever you want.</i>

699
00:49:39,768 --> 00:49:41,603
<i>I can do whatever I want.</i>

700
00:49:42,145 --> 00:49:43,855
<i>I want to hear it straight</i>
<i>from your mouth.</i>

701
00:49:43,939 --> 00:49:45,774
<i>You're Lily Cruz, right?</i>

702
00:49:46,358 --> 00:49:49,486
<i>Yes, I'm Lily Cruz!</i>

703
00:49:50,696 --> 00:49:53,699
[theme music playing]
